# React Conventions

## Placement & naming

- Put interactive UI in `src/components/` — `auth/` for forms, `ui/` for reusable primitives.
- One component per file; filename `PascalCase.tsx` matching the component name.
- Use `@/` path alias for imports (e.g. `@/components/ui/button`, `@/lib/utils`).
- Prefer **named exports** for building blocks; **default export** only for top-level page islands (e.g. `SignInForm`).

## Components & types

- Functional components only; type props with `interface ComponentNameProps` (or `Props` for a single exported form).
- Use `import type { ReactNode } from "react"` for type-only imports.
- Prefix intentionally unused identifiers with `_` (ESLint).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — typed props, named export
interface FormFieldProps {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  onChange: (value: string) => void;
}

export function FormField({ id, label, onChange }: FormFieldProps) { /* ... */ }
```

## Styling

- Tailwind utility classes; merge conditionals with `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- Shared primitives in `ui/` use `class-variance-authority` (`cva`) + `VariantProps` (see `button.tsx`).
- Icons from `lucide-react` with `className="size-4"` (or `size-3` for inline hints).

## Astro integration

- React runs as **client islands** in `.astro` pages — add `client:load` (or stricter directive when appropriate).
- Keep routes and layouts as `.astro`; do not convert pages to `.tsx` unless required.
- Forms may use native `method`/`action` to API routes; client-side validation runs in `onSubmit` before submit.

## Hooks & React 19

- Follow Rules of Hooks; only call hooks at the top level of function components or custom hooks.
- `react-compiler` is an **error** — write code the compiler can optimize (no manual memoization unless needed).
- Use `useFormStatus` from `react-dom` inside submit buttons wrapped by a `<form>`.
- Prefer `React.SubmitEvent<HTMLFormElement>` for form submit handlers.

## Accessibility

- jsx-a11y rules apply — associate labels with inputs (`htmlFor` + `id`), meaningful `aria-label` on icon-only controls.
- Do not rely on color alone for errors; show text (see `FormField` error pattern).

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — accessible toggle
<button type="button" onClick={onToggle} aria-label={visible ? "Hide password" : "Show password"}>
```

## Before finishing

- Run `npm run lint` on touched files.
- Manually verify affected routes (e.g. `/auth/signin`, `/auth/signup`) when changing auth components.
